    </version>
    <date>
      <![CDATA[]]>
    </date>
    <status>
      <![CDATA[]]>
    </status>
    <prefix>
      <![CDATA[]]>
    </prefix>
    <confidence>
      <![CDATA[false]]>
    </confidence>
    <note>
      <![CDATA[]]>
    </note>
  </properties>

  <gsn>
    <g
        id="__gsn__1955dbc0a99"
        color="#ffcccc"
        name="Correct Implementation of the Solution">
      The OpenUxAS Zone Violation Alert Service is a correct implementation of the proposed Zone Alert Service solution.

      <s
          id="__gsn__1955dd78f65"
          color="#ffcccc"
          name="Strategy">
        Through design of the algorithm and testing of its output against representative cases.

        <g
            id="__gsn__1955dd79465"
            color="#ffcccc"
            name="Algorithmic Correctness">
          The ZoneAlertService provides an OpenUxAS service to make OpenUxAS systems aware of potential for future zone violations by vehicles based on zone and vehicle positions and vehicle behavior

          <c
              id="__gsn__195959fee60"
              color="#ccffff"
              name="Req HL-1-1">
            .
          </c>

          <s
              id="__gsn__1955dbc3b64"
              color="#ffcccc"
              name="Strategy">
            Each of the high level requirements for the system is satisfied by steps of the algorithm.

            <j
                id="__gsn__19581b97846"
                color="#ffffff"
                name="Justification">
              That requirements transitively show correct computation of zone alerts that reflect the interpretation of zones as reflected in the validity of the RoutePlannerVisibilityService.
            </j>

            <m
                id="__gsn__1955dc4284a"
                color="#ffcccc"
                name="Satisfies HL-1-1-1">
              The service computes and applies zones of the same geometry computed and applied by the RoutePlannerVisibilityService.

              <c
                  id="__gsn__19581bd3de4"
                  color="#ccffff"
                  name="Req HL-1-1-1">
                .
              </c>
            </m>

            <m
                id="__gsn__1955dc42aae"
                color="#ffcccc"
                name="Satisfies HL-1-1-2">
              The service correctly and accurately reports zone violations from vehicle state reports and computed zone geometry

              <c
                  id="__gsn__19581bcd541"
                  color="#ccffff"
                  name="Req HL-1-1-2">
              </c>
            </m>

            <m
                id="__gsn__1955de31cb3"
                color="#cdcdcd"
                name="Satisfies HL-1-1-3">
              The service correctly declares all zones it constructs for zone alerting in a timely manner before mission start.

              <c
                  id="__gsn__19581bd027c"
                  color="#ccffff"
                  name="Req HL-1-1-3">
                .
              </c>
            </m>
          </s>
        </g>

        <g
            id="__gsn__1955dd798cd"
            color="#cdcdcd"
            name="Integration Test Results">
          The ZoneAlertService correctly emits all and only alerts for reported VehicleState messages against use-representative collections of declared zones.

          <e
              id="__gsn__1955dde01a9"
              color="#cdcdcd"
              name="Full Integration Tests">
            Tests of the ZoneAlertService for declared vehicle state messages against representative scenarios with declared zones shows that vehicles report zone violations as intended by the definitions of existing and immediate zone violations for keep-in and keep-out zones.
          </e>
        </g>
      </s>
    </g>
  </gsn>
</argument>
